   "properties": {
    "id": "feature:skaguay-pipeline-b",
    "name": "Skaguay pipeline, across the side valley (line followed, less sure)",
    "kind": "pipeline",
    "grade": "inferred",
    "error_ft": 80,
    "length_ft": 3787,
    "basis": "The same thin line continues, but here it drops about 100 ft to the floor of a side valley, runs along its edge at about 8,750 ft, and climbs again to about 8,790 ft. A stave pipe under pressure could cross a valley so, as a sag; a footpath would also look like this. The line is continuous with the stretches either side, which is the reason for taking it as the pipe. Less sure than those.",
